Implemented:
- Private supervisor and logic entry points, each owning bbt-rt. One bounded startup JSON line carries the private GUI root/capability and public identity status; no capability/secret in argv or logs.
- IO owns both processes and one admitted GUI connection. Control pipes live outside Child because Tokio Child::wait closes child.stdin on its first poll, even if cancelled. Explicit async close reaps both; timeouts are errors. Default macOS Quit menu is disabled so Command-Q reaches this path.
- gui.sock shares the existing owner/mode/version/capability/1MiB framing. Subscribe before initial status/list; multiplex state for unwatched seats and ack-gated optional views; resync status/list on bus gap. Existing seat MCP control preserved.
- GUI logic maps adapter/lifecycle state, cached supervisor process metadata, launch planner, operator input and bounded resize. UI publishes immutable models through Grids/build/apply state/prepare before Applied. No production Screen content reads in C1a.
- Production logic uses start_custodied. Pending identity is public state/reason in Ready, GuiReply::Identity, the immutable model and a one-line sidebar footer. Kestrel ID1d owns custody/retry/held queue/audit.
